message: "If you use this data or code, please cite it as below, together with the associated article."
title: "Stable cores and marginal churn: reliability of a single-year exceedance indicator across India's river monitoring network, 2016-2024 (data and code)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Ranjit
    affiliation: "Leuphana University Lüneburg"
version: "rev20"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Harmonized station-year dataset of India's National Water Quality Monitoring Programme river stations
  (CPCB annual reports, 2016-2024; 1,891 stations), linked monthly records, context variables, and the
  complete Python and R pipeline that tests the reliability of single-year exceedance status as a
  water-quality indicator.
keywords:
  - water quality
  - status indicator
  - compliance assessment
  - measurement uncertainty
  - monitoring network
  - India
